Constructor chaining is the process of calling one constructor from within another constructor.
This occurs with the help of this() and super() calling statements.
In the same class one constructor can call another one using this() statement while in different classes one constructor can call another using super() statement.
These this() and super() statements must be written in the first line within the calling constructor, such that the constructor is invoked/called even before the
execution of the constructor that called it. 
